// =====================================================================
// THE CATALOG CARD SET -- 105 cards, none of whose content is written
// here.
//
// Every class in this file is four lines: it names a bestiary family, a
// registry theme, or a PACK axis, and inherits everything else from
// RS_Upgrade_CatalogBases.zsc. That is deliberate. The behaviour of a
// Levy card is one implementation shared by thirteen cards; the thing
// that makes LevyRevenant different from LevyImp is a single string
// that RS_MinionCatalog resolves at runtime.
//
// Which means the card set grows when the CATALOGS grow, not when this
// file is edited. Add a monster to RS_MinionCatalog and five cards get
// deeper. Tag an FX actor in RS_FXRegistry and up to five more do.
//
//   FAMILY x13  Levy / Horde / Bane / Tithe / Cull      = 65
//   THEME  x8   Brand / Attune / Surge                  = 24
//   AXIS   x8   Flourish / Echo                         = 16
//                                                        ---
//                                                        105
//
// SOUND is the ninth PACK axis and has no cards, because RS_FXRegistry
// currently holds zero entries on that axis -- a sound card would draw
// null every time. It comes back the moment sounds are registered.
//
// GENERATED SHAPE, HAND-OWNED CONTENT: the classes below are uniform on
// purpose so that a bug is fixed once in the base. Do not add per-card
// behaviour here; add it to the base and let all thirteen inherit it.
// =====================================================================

class TFLV_Upgrade_RS_LevyPinky : RS_CatCard_ConscriptBase
{
	override string Family() { return "demon"; }
	override bool IsSuitableForWeapon(TFLV_WeaponInfo info)
	{ return CardTakeable(info, "TFLV_Upgrade_RS_LevyPinky"); }
}

